# PNG to WebP

## Scope

- MUST apply when the agent adds or updates a **shipping** `.png`, or leaves a shipping path pointing at `.png`.
- MUST NOT auto-convert under `tmp/`, `node_modules/`, `.git/`, `vendor/`, or other clearly vendored / scratch trees unless the user points at a file there.
- MUST NOT treat intermediate build scratch (for example a temp PNG before encode) as a shipping asset.

## When a shipping PNG appears

- MUST convert each in-scope `.png` to `.webp` before finishing the task, unless the user explicitly asks to keep PNG.
- MUST use **`cwebp`** from libwebp, for example `cwebp -q 85 in.png -o out.webp`. If `cwebp` is missing, MUST report that and stop or ask for an approved alternative; MUST NOT silently skip.
- MUST update every reference to the old `.png` path in the files touched for that change (markdown, HTML, CSS, config, code strings, and sibling locale copies when present).
- SHOULD remove the original `.png` after a successful convert and reference update, unless the user asks to keep it.
- MAY leave `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, and existing `.webp` unchanged unless the user asks to recompress or convert those too.

## Verify

- MUST run the project's documented build or check (for example `make build`, `hugo`, or the nearest test that loads the asset) after path changes so broken references surface immediately.
